sequenceDiagram
  %% Record-only detach: the Gateway action and shared admission guards.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:node-service:detach
  %% kind: instance.node_service_detach
  autonumber
  %% lane CALL icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  participant CALL as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  Note over CALL: Resolve input and consent
  %%> When:
  %%> - An omitted Instance uses registry choices; an omitted attachment ID is typed from the attach result because no attachment list is available. Invalid typed IDs are prompted again before consent.
  alt local input refused
    CALL--xCALL: Refused or cancelled<br/>No delete request
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - instance.id_invalid refuses an invalid supplied or missing noninteractive Instance ID, or an empty Instance list after the registry GET; no mutation request is sent.
    %%> - instance.node_service_target_id_invalid refuses an invalid supplied attachment ID or an omitted attachment ID in JSON or noninteractive mode. An omitted terminal attachment ID is prompted, with validation retries before consent.
    %%> - instance.node_service_confirmation_required refuses a JSON or noninteractive call without --yes.
    %%> - input.cancelled ends a cancelled terminal selection, attachment-ID prompt or declined consent before mutation.
    %%> - State stays unchanged. Invalid supplied IDs, missing noninteractive IDs and missing noninteractive consent send no request. A terminal Instance selection can follow a registry read.
  else inputs and consent ready
    CALL->>GW: instance:node-service<br/>detach INSTANCE TARGET
    %%> Command:
    %%> - orbit instance:node-service:detach INSTANCE TARGET
    %%> - syntax: instance:node-service:detach
    Note over GW: Check request and access
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - peer.identity_unknown or node_access.required (403): the caller lacks authority.
    %%> - http.404 (404): the Instance cannot be resolved.
    %%> - validation.failed (422) or operation.idempotency_conflict (409): the request key is invalid or conflicts.
    %%> - Every refusal leaves state unchanged and creates no new receipt.
    alt request or access refused
      GW--xCALL: Request refused<br/>No changes or new receipt
    else request admitted
      Note over GW: Lock the Instance<br/>Begin one transaction
      alt lifecycle busy
        GW--xCALL: Lifecycle busy<br/>No changes or new receipt
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - instance.lifecycle_busy (409): the Instance is not active, migration is running or a detach is already running.
      else failed move retains runtime
        GW--xCALL: Runtime cleanup required<br/>No changes or new receipt
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - instance.node_service_runtime_cleanup_required (409): retry instance:migrate to finish or restore the move before detaching.
      else target missing or foreign
        GW--xCALL: Attachment missing (404)<br/>No changes or new receipt
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - instance.node_service_target_missing: the attachment must belong to the selected Instance.
      else another Operation owns target
        GW--xCALL: Target busy<br/>No changes or new receipt
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - operation.target_busy (409): the Instance's Operation lock is held.
      else target admitted
        Note over GW: Remove attachment<br/>Record succeeded Operation
        %%> When:
        %%> - The Instance uses its checkout or has completed migration successfully.
        alt transaction fails
          GW--xCALL: Transaction failed<br/>Both writes roll back
          %%> On failure:
          %%> - The attachment remains and no new receipt is persisted, including no failed receipt.
        else transaction commits
          GW-->>CALL: Completed Operation
        end
      end
    end
  end
